WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
ASDRP / EEG EYE STATE
Can short-term history decode a neural state?
A time-aware classification study using a public 14-channel EEG recording.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
THE DATA
14 channels. 14,980 samples.
One continuous recording with a manually annotated open-eye / closed-eye label.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
THE EVALUATION
Time order matters.
70% train, 15% validation, 15% final test. No random row split.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
THE BASELINE
Test ROC AUC: 0.625
Pointwise standardized EEG with class-balanced logistic regression.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
THE EXTENSION
Test ROC AUC: 0.530
Causal temporal context did not generalize on the final held-out block.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
THE EXPANSION
Five blocked folds stay near chance.
Mean ROC AUC: 0.478 pointwise versus 0.488 with context; fold variation is wide.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
THE LIMIT
Negative results count.
More recordings and multiple time scales are needed before generalization claims.

